# suite=runner; columns: <FAULT_ID> <must-fail> <allowed-prefixes> <must-pass>
# Runner outcome named faults (D-20, D-24, plan 04-03). Each id has one IVS_FAULT_<ID> site in
# runner/outcome.c (owner TUs under core/ or runner/).
# OUTCOME_GUEST_AS_HARNESS: guest-fail exits with the harness-fail code; codes-distinct also
# sees the two outcomes share code 14.
OUTCOME_GUEST_AS_HARNESS runner.outcome.exit-guest-fail runner.outcome.exit-guest-fail|runner.outcome.codes-distinct runner.outcome.exit-pass
# OUTCOME_TIMEOUT_AS_GUEST: both timeout kinds exit with the guest-fail code; codes-distinct
# also sees timeout and guest-fail share code 10.
OUTCOME_TIMEOUT_AS_GUEST runner.outcome.exit-timeout runner.outcome.exit-timeout|runner.outcome.codes-distinct runner.outcome.exit-pass
# OUTCOME_MISSING_FIXTURE_EXIT0: missing-fixture exits 0 (a missing file would read as a pass);
# codes-distinct also sees it share code 0 with pass.
OUTCOME_MISSING_FIXTURE_EXIT0 runner.outcome.exit-missing-fixture runner.outcome.exit-missing-fixture|runner.outcome.codes-distinct runner.outcome.exit-pass
# OUTCOME_CANCEL_AS_TIMEOUT: resolve ranks cancelled below the wall timeout; only the pair case
# that holds both observations sees it (each alone still resolves to itself).
OUTCOME_CANCEL_AS_TIMEOUT runner.outcome.prec-cancelled-over-wall runner.outcome.prec-cancelled-over-wall runner.outcome.prec-wall-over-budget
